>> title: Đồ Chua
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: daikon, carrot, vietnamese, pickle, banh mi
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: do chua, pickled carrots and daikon, pickled carrot and daikon, pickled daikon and carrots, Vietnamese pickles, banh mi pickles, pickles
>> pairs-with: baguette, banh-xeo
>> servings: 12
>> time: 25 hr
>> step.1: salt 20 min, rinse and squeeze dry
>> step.2: stir the brine
>> step.3: pack the jar, brine 1 hr
>> step.4: chill 24 hr

Toss @daikon{1%lb}(450 g; 3-in matchsticks) and @carrots{2%medium}(225 g; 3-in matchsticks) with @kosher salt{2%tsp} and @sugar{2%tsp}, ~stand{20%min} until a stick bends without snapping, then rinse and squeeze dry. The salt is rinsed away — it is there to pull the water out, not to season.

Stir @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g) and @fine sea salt{1%tsp} into @warm water{1%cup}(240 mL) until dissolved, then add @distilled white vinegar{1 1/4%cup}(300 mL).

Pack @&(~2)vegetables{} into a #2-quart jar{} and pour @&(~1)brine{} over to cover, ~brine{1%hr} on the counter.

Refrigerate @&(~1)pickles{} ~chill{24%hr}; they keep 4 weeks in the fridge.
